Bugfix: Remove a dead rule for enabled submit buttons

A rule for submit buttons carrying the class "enabled" declared a green border
on a green fill and was reported as a contrast violation. The class is never
put on an input anywhere in the codebase, so no browser has ever applied the
rule. It arrived years ago when the form styles moved between stylesheets and
its user did not come along.

Recolouring unreachable code would have closed the report without changing
anything, so the rule was removed.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.4.11
